---
/**
 * pages/entity/[noun]/[id].astro
 *
 * Detail route for the three D1-backed entity types (composer, composition, contributor) — the SSG
 * analog of `[...slug].astro` for the EmDash pages/posts world, but simpler: an entity record has no
 * per-record template pointer, so every record of one noun renders through that noun's `is_default`
 * `design_template` (entity-routes.ts). Matches the existing `/entity/{noun}/{id}` link convention
 * already emitted by `ListResult.astro`, so that pointer resolves with zero change there.
 *
 * Dual-source dependency (impl plan Step 6): a page needs BOTH a resolved default template (EmDash) and
 * at least one D1 record for that noun. Either being absent — unconfigured D1, unconfigured CMS, no
 * default template authored yet, or an empty table — skips that noun's pages for this build, not a
 * build failure. This lets a bootstrap build (neither configured) still pass.
 *
 * Lint runs once per noun, not once per record: no error-severity lint rule varies across records of
 * one noun. `dangling-outlet-field` keys on `entityFields(noun)`, which is static per noun (not a live
 * per-record schema read). Heading order comes only from the template's own components — entity outlets
 * inject no Portable Text headings of their own — so it cannot differ between two records of the same
 * template. One representative record (the first fetched) is passed as `entry` so `lintDesign`'s
 * entry-gated heading-order check runs at all (it is skipped when `context.entry` is null, mirroring
 * "the build always pairs an entry").
 *
 * Unified field-outlet rewrite: `resolveEntityTemplates(entityTemplates)` is computed ONCE, up front,
 * because `buildReferenceIndex` needs to know — for ALL THREE nouns at once — whether composer and
 * contributor each resolve to a published default template this build (a composition's `composer`/
 * `contrib_*` reference fields link to a public page only when their target noun actually gets one).
 * `entityRecords`'s per-noun loop below reuses that same resolution.
